>1</fpage><lpage>17</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b009"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Holtgrave</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Costs and consequences of the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention's recommendations for opt-out HIV testing</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>e194</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.pmed.0040194">10.1371/journal.pmed.0040194</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17564488</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b010"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kamb</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Fishbein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Douglas</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rhodes</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Efficacy of risk-reduction counseling to prevent Human Immunodeficiency Virus and sexually transmitted diseases</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>280</volume><fpage>1161</fpage><lpage>1167</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9777816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab><year>2001</year><article-title>Revised guidelines for HIV counseling, testing, and referral</article-title><source>MMWR Recomm Rep</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>57</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Valdiserri</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The continued spread of HIV in the United States: Prevention failure or systems defect?</article-title><source>J Public Health Manag Pract</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>586</fpage><lpage>589</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17041308</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b013"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Maciosek</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Coffield</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Flottemesch</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Priorities among effective clinical preventive services: Results of a systematic review and analysis</article-title><source>Am J Prev Med</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>52</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16777543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040200-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Glasgow</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Orleans</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Curry</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Solberg</surname><given-names>LI</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Does the chronic care model serve also as a template for improving prevention?</article-title><source>Milbank Q</source><volume>79</volume><fpage>579</fpage><lpage>612</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11789118</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><glossary><title>Abbreviations</title><def-list><def-item><term>CDC</term><def><p>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</p></def></def-item></def-list></glossary><fn-group><fn id="n3" fn-type="current-aff"><p>Ronald O. Valdiserri is in the US Department of Veterans Affairs, Washington, D. C., United States of America. E-mail: <email>R.Valdiserri&#x00040;va.gov</email></p></fn><fn id="n1" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> The author received no specific funding for this article.</p></fn><fn id="n2" fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests:</bold> The author wishes to declare that he was employed by the United States Centers for Disease Control and Prevention at the time that the guidelines discussed in this article were developed and was involved in their review. Also, the author has in the past collaborated professionally on several occasions with Dr. Holtgrave. The opinions expressed in this commentary are those of the author and do not necessarily represent the views of the US Department of Veterans Affairs.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>